@clawsweeper re-review

The branch and evidence are current. Exact-head CI and independent review pass. Four twenty-minute untraced controls and two swapped candidate comparisons resolve the earlier GC/latency concern without a rejecting regression. Patch-owner allocation improves 12.2–24.3%, and transfer bytes per patch fall 86.0%.

The body retains the separate promotion limitation: identical-source trace controls are unstable, the longer screen stopped explicitly at two of four planned controls, and no valid candidate promotion comparison is claimed. Landing relies on the scoped allocation benefit, correctness, and valid untraced cost evidence.
